Here what we actually do that we dont iterate on the actual array
but we find the search space for the given array and try to find the answer from the search space
For Example:
 public static int shipWithinDays(int[] weights, int days) {
        int start =Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        int end =0;
        for(int w : weights){
            start = Math.max(start, w);
            end +=w;
        }
        int ans =-1;
        while(start <= end){
            int mid = start +((end-start)/2);
            if(isShippingPossible(weights, mid, days)){
                ans = mid;
                end = mid -1;
            }else{
                start = mid +1;
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }
    public static boolean isShippingPossible(int[] arr, int minimumWeight, int totalDays){
        int days =1;
        int totalWeight =0;
        for(int w : arr){
            totalWeight+=w;
            if(totalWeight>minimumWeight){
                totalWeight = w;
                days++;
            }if(days>totalDays){
                return false;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }


 In this code we first find the search Space
 which is here (MaxElementOfTheArray, TotalSumArray) (start = MaxElementOfTheArray, end=TotalSumArray)
 then we will apply the binarySearch on this Search Space
 find the middle if it qualifies the condition(isShippingPossible(weights, mid, days))
 then we will mark it as an potential answer and continue the search in the search space until we find the monotonic answer(After which the answer is same)